# SPA fallback.
#
# Every route on this site — /projects, /services, /systems, /contact — is
# rendered by React Router in the browser. Nothing matching them exists on
# disk, so a reader who opens one directly, refreshes on one, or follows a
# shared link would otherwise get Netlify's 404 instead of the page.
#
# Netlify serves real files first, so this never shadows /assets or the
# favicon; it only catches paths that would have 404'd. The 200 keeps the URL
# in the bar so the router can read it and render the right route.
/*    /index.html    200
